Add Saffron goal supervision

Idle root goals need a lightweight watchdog without changing Codex durable
goal ownership.

Add a process-local supervisor that creates one bounded, hidden, full-history
helper for an active root goal. Hidden helpers neither appear in user agent
lists nor consume normal agent capacity, and their privileged actions are
authorized by registry identity rather than a role name. The supervisor owns
its communication with the parent, so Codex does not also enqueue ordinary
child-completion messages.

The helper can resume its parent, snooze with capped retry backoff, compact
parent context, or complete the goal. Snoozes are reserved for future
deadlines and already-running non-human processes; user questions and
internal decisions wake the parent instead. Every snooze records the process
or scheduled boundary that justifies it.

Give root threads one persistent lifecycle contract while Goals and Saffron
supervision are enabled. World State restores the guidance after compaction
and resume without duplication. When an idle goal cannot acquire a supervisor
owner, fall back to ordinary goal continuation.

Cover hidden-helper accounting, authority checks, supervisor runtime behavior,
root guidance across ordinary turns, compaction and resume, and the app-server
lifecycle.
